# Testing Guide

## Test Structure

### Directory Organization
```
test/
├── core/                   # Core functionality tests
│   ├── providers/         # Provider tests
│   ├── utils/             # Utility function tests
│   └── error_handling/    # Error handling tests
├── features/              # Feature tests
│   ├── onboarding/        # Onboarding feature tests
│   ├── transaction/       # Transaction feature tests
│   └── wallets/           # Wallet feature tests
├── shared/                # Shared functionality tests
│   ├── services/          # Service tests
│   └── ui_components/     # UI component tests
├── perf/                  # Performance tests
└── widget_test.dart      # Main widget test
```

## Unit Testing

### 1. Provider Testing
```dart
import 'package:flutter_test/flutter_test.dart';
import 'package:flutter_riverpod/flutter_riverpod.dart';
import 'package:pocketa/features/transaction/presentation/viewmodels/transaction_providers.dart';

void main() {
  group('Transaction Providers', () {
    late ProviderContainer container;
    
    setUp(() {
      container = ProviderContainer();
    });
    
    tearDown(() {
      container.dispose();
    });
    
    test('should return initial state', () {
      final state = container.read(transactionProvider);
      expect(state.isLoading, false);
      expect(state.transactions, isEmpty);
    });
    
    test('should load transactions', () async {
      // Mock repository
      final mockRepository = MockTransactionRepository();
      when(mockRepository.getAll()).thenAnswer((_) async => [mockTransaction]);
      
      // Override provider
      container = ProviderContainer(
        overrides: [
          transactionRepositoryProvider.overrideWithValue(mockRepository),
        ],
      );
      
      // Test loading
      final notifier = container.read(transactionProvider.notifier);
      await notifier.loadTransactions();
      
      final state = container.read(transactionProvider);
      expect(state.transactions, hasLength(1));
      expect(state.isLoading, false);
    });
  });
}
```

### 2. Repository Testing
```dart
import 'package:hive/hive.dart';
import 'package:pocketa/features/transaction/data/transaction_repo_impl.dart';

void main() {
  group('TransactionRepository', () {
    late Box<Transaction> mockBox;
    late TransactionRepositoryImpl repository;
    
    setUp(() {
      mockBox = MockBox<Transaction>();
      repository = TransactionRepositoryImpl(mockBox);
    });
    
    test('should return all transactions', () {
      final transactions = [transaction1, transaction2];
      when(mockBox.values).thenReturn(transactions);
      
      final result = repository.getAll();
      
      expect(result, equals(transactions));
    });
    
    test('should add transaction', () {
      when(mockBox.add(any)).thenAnswer((_) async => 0);
      
      repository.add(transaction);
      
      verify(mockBox.add(transaction)).called(1);
    });
  });
}
```

### 3. Use Case Testing
```dart
import 'package:pocketa/features/transaction/domain/usecases/get_transactions.dart';

void main() {
  group('GetTransactions', () {
    late MockTransactionRepository mockRepository;
    late GetTransactions useCase;
    
    setUp(() {
      mockRepository = MockTransactionRepository();
      useCase = GetTransactions(mockRepository);
    });
    
    test('should return transactions when repository succeeds', () async {
      // Arrange
      final transactions = [transaction1, transaction2];
      when(mockRepository.getAll()).thenAnswer((_) async => transactions);
      
      // Act
      final result = await useCase();
      
      // Assert
      expect(result, equals(transactions));
      verify(mockRepository.getAll()).called(1);
    });
    
    test('should throw exception when repository fails', () async {
      // Arrange
      when(mockRepository.getAll()).thenThrow(Exception('Database error'));
      
      // Act & Assert
      expect(() => useCase(), throwsException);
    });
  });
}
```

## Widget Testing

### 1. Basic Widget Tests
```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';
import 'package:flutter_test/flutter_test.dart';
import 'package:pocketa/shared/ui_components/buttons/app_button.dart';

void main() {
  group('AppButton', () {
    testWidgets('should display text', (tester) async {
      await tester.pumpWidget(
        MaterialApp(
          home: AppButton(
            text: 'Test Button',
            onPressed: () {},
          ),
        ),
      );
      
      expect(find.text('Test Button'), findsOneWidget);
    });
    
    testWidgets('should call onPressed when tapped', (tester) async {
      bool pressed = false;
      
      await tester.pumpWidget(
        MaterialApp(
          home: AppButton(
            text: 'Test Button',
            onPressed: () => pressed = true,
          ),
        ),
      );
      
      await tester.tap(find.text('Test Button'));
      expect(pressed, true);
    });
    
    testWidgets('should show loading state', (tester) async {
      await tester.pumpWidget(
        MaterialApp(
          home: AppButton(
            text: 'Test Button',
            onPressed: () {},
            isLoading: true,
          ),
        ),
      );
      
      expect(find.byType(CircularProgressIndicator), findsOneWidget);
      expect(find.text('Test Button'), findsNothing);
    });
  });
}
```

### 2. Consumer Widget Tests
```dart
import 'package:flutter_riverpod/flutter_riverpod.dart';
import 'package:pocketa/features/transaction/presentation/pages/transaction_screen.dart';

void main() {
  group('TransactionScreen', () {
    testWidgets('should display transactions', (tester) async {
      final mockTransactions = [transaction1, transaction2];
      
      await tester.pumpWidget(
        ProviderScope(
          overrides: [
            allTransactionsProvider.overrideWithValue(
              AsyncValue.data(mockTransactions),
            ),
          ],
          child: MaterialApp(
            home: TransactionScreen(),
          ),
        ),
      );
      
      expect(find.text('Transaction 1'), findsOneWidget);
      expect(find.text('Transaction 2'), findsOneWidget);
    });
    
    testWidgets('should show loading indicator', (tester) async {
      await tester.pumpWidget(
        ProviderScope(
          overrides: [
            allTransactionsProvider.overrideWithValue(
              const AsyncValue.loading(),
            ),
          ],
          child: MaterialApp(
            home: TransactionScreen(),
          ),
        ),
      );
      
      expect(find.byType(CircularProgressIndicator), findsOneWidget);
    });
    
    testWidgets('should show error message', (tester) async {
      await tester.pumpWidget(
        ProviderScope(
          overrides: [
            allTransactionsProvider.overrideWithValue(
              AsyncValue.error('Error message', StackTrace.current),
            ),
          ],
          child: MaterialApp(
            home: TransactionScreen(),
          ),
        ),
      );
      
      expect(find.text('Error message'), findsOneWidget);
    });
  });
}
```

### 3. Form Testing
```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';
import 'package:flutter_test/flutter_test.dart';
import 'package:pocketa/features/transaction/presentation/widgets/transaction_form.dart';

void main() {
  group('TransactionForm', () {
    testWidgets('should validate required fields', (tester) async {
      await tester.pumpWidget(
        MaterialApp(
          home: TransactionForm(),
        ),
      );
      
      // Try to submit without filling fields
      await tester.tap(find.text('Save'));
      await tester.pump();
      
      expect(find.text('Amount is required'), findsOneWidget);
      expect(find.text('Category is required'), findsOneWidget);
    });
    
    testWidgets('should submit form when valid', (tester) async {
      bool submitted = false;
      
      await tester.pumpWidget(
        MaterialApp(
          home: TransactionForm(
            onSubmit: () => submitted = true,
          ),
        ),
      );
      
      // Fill form
      await tester.enterText(find.byKey(Key('amount_field')), '100');
      await tester.tap(find.byKey(Key('category_dropdown')));
      await tester.pumpAndSettle();
      await tester.tap(find.text('Food'));
      await tester.pumpAndSettle();
      
      // Submit
      await tester.tap(find.text('Save'));
      await tester.pump();
      
      expect(submitted, true);
    });
  });
}
```

## Integration Testing

### 1. Feature Integration Tests
```dart
import 'package:flutter_test/flutter_test.dart';
import 'package:integration_test/integration_test.dart';
import 'package:pocketa/main.dart' as app;

void main() {
  IntegrationTestWidgetsFlutterBinding.ensureInitialized();
  
  group('Transaction Flow', () {
    testWidgets('should add transaction', (tester) async {
      app.main();
      await tester.pumpAndSettle();
      
      // Navigate to add transaction
      await tester.tap(find.text('Add Transaction'));
      await tester.pumpAndSettle();
      
      // Fill form
      await tester.enterText(find.byKey(Key('amount_field')), '50.00');
      await tester.tap(find.byKey(Key('category_dropdown')));
      await tester.pumpAndSettle();
      await tester.tap(find.text('Food'));
      await tester.pumpAndSettle();
      
      // Submit
      await tester.tap(find.text('Save'));
      await tester.pumpAndSettle();
      
      // Verify transaction was added
      expect(find.text('50.00'), findsOneWidget);
      expect(find.text('Food'), findsOneWidget);
    });
  });
}
```

## Performance Testing

### 1. Widget Performance Tests
```dart
import 'package:flutter_test/flutter_test.dart';
import 'package:pocketa/shared/ui_components/lists/optimized_list_view.dart';

void main() {
  group('OptimizedListView Performance', () {
    testWidgets('should render within performance budget', (tester) async {
      final stopwatch = Stopwatch()..start();
      
      await tester.pumpWidget(
        MaterialApp(
          home: OptimizedListView(
            itemCount: 1000,
            itemBuilder: (context, index) => ListTile(
              title: Text('Item $index'),
            ),
          ),
        ),
      );
      
      await tester.pumpAndSettle();
      stopwatch.stop();
      
      expect(stopwatch.elapsedMilliseconds, lessThan(100));
    });
  });
}
```

### 2. Memory Tests
```dart
import 'dart:io';
import 'package:flutter_test/flutter_test.dart';

void main() {
  group('Memory Tests', () {
    test('should not leak memory', () async {
      final initialMemory = ProcessInfo.currentRss;
      
      // Perform operations that might leak memory
      for (int i = 0; i < 1000; i++) {
        await performOperation();
      }
      
      // Force garbage collection
      await Future.delayed(Duration(seconds: 1));
      
      final finalMemory = ProcessInfo.currentRss;
      expect(finalMemory - initialMemory, lessThan(10 * 1024 * 1024)); // 10MB
    });
  });
}
```

## Mock Objects

### 1. Mock Repository
```dart
class MockTransactionRepository extends Mock implements TransactionRepository {}

class MockBox<T> extends Mock implements Box<T> {
  @override
  Iterable<T> get values => throw UnimplementedError();
  
  @override
  Future<int> add(T item) async => 0;
  
  @override
  Future<void> put(String key, T item) async {}
  
  @override
  T? get(String key) => null;
}
```

### 2. Mock Provider
```dart
class MockTransactionNotifier extends StateNotifier<TransactionState> {
  MockTransactionNotifier() : super(TransactionState.initial());
  
  void mockLoadTransactions() {
    state = state.copyWith(
      transactions: [mockTransaction1, mockTransaction2],
      isLoading: false,
    );
  }
  
  void mockError(String error) {
    state = state.copyWith(
      error: error,
      isLoading: false,
    );
  }
}
```

## Test Utilities

### 1. Test Helpers
```dart
class TestHelpers {
  static Widget createTestApp({Widget? home, List<Override>? overrides}) {
    return ProviderScope(
      overrides: overrides ?? [],
      child: MaterialApp(
        home: home ?? const SizedBox(),
        localizationsDelegates: AppLocalizations.localizationsDelegates,
        supportedLocales: AppLocalizations.supportedLocales,
      ),
    );
  }
  
  static Future<void> pumpAndSettle(WidgetTester tester) async {
    await tester.pump();
    await tester.pumpAndSettle();
  }
  
  static Transaction createMockTransaction({
    String id = '1',
    double amount = 100.0,
    String category = 'Food',
  }) {
    return Transaction(
      id: id,
      amount: amount,
      category: category,
      createdAt: DateTime.now(),
    );
  }
}
```

### 2. Custom Matchers
```dart
Matcher hasTransactionWithAmount(double amount) {
  return predicate<Transaction>(
    (transaction) => transaction.amount == amount,
    'has transaction with amount $amount',
  );
}

Matcher hasError(String error) {
  return predicate<AsyncValue>(
    (value) => value.hasError && value.error.toString().contains(error),
    'has error containing "$error"',
  );
}
```

## Best Practices

### 1. Test Organization
- Group related tests using `group()`
- Use descriptive test names
- Follow AAA pattern (Arrange, Act, Assert)

### 2. Test Data
- Use factories for creating test data
- Keep test data minimal and focused
- Use meaningful test data values

### 3. Mocking
- Mock external dependencies
- Verify interactions with mocks
- Use realistic mock responses

### 4. Performance
- Test performance-critical code
- Set performance budgets
- Monitor memory usage

### 5. Coverage
- Aim for high test coverage
- Focus on critical business logic
- Test edge cases and error conditions